#: ../../../introduction/external-documentation.rst:3
#: 33411aa91d3f4c7bb6d9de1ef19e9844
msgid "About external documentation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../introduction/external-documentation.rst:7
#: c50fbfa3118a4d4da0166f6699933508
msgid ""
"**External documentation is not maintained by the Qubes OS Project.** "
"Content linked from the Qubes documentation was reviewed when the link was "
"added to the index, but nothing prevents the content from being edited at "
"any time. You should carefully review any external content before applying "
"it to your system. You do this at your own risk."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../introduction/external-documentation.rst:10
#: f422f93991904d9796c90e5b8dfc05c0
msgid ""
"**Core documentation** resides in the `Qubes OS Project’s official "
"repositories <https://github.com/QubesOS/>`__, mainly in `qubes-doc <https://"
"github.com/QubesOS/qubes-doc>`__. **External documentation** can be anywhere "
"else (such as forums, community websites, and blogs), but there is an "
"especially large collection in the `Qubes Forum <https://forum.qubes-os.org/"
"docs>`__. The main difference between **core** (or **official**) and "
"**external** (or **community** or **unofficial**) documentation is whether "
"**it documents software that is officially written and maintained by the "
"Qubes OS Project**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../introduction/external-documentation.rst:13
#: 147ba61297a146779f02078647986319
msgid ""
"The purpose of this distinction is **to keep the core docs maintainable and "
"high-quality** by limiting them to the software output by the Qubes OS "
"Project. In other words, **we take responsibility for documenting all of the "
"software we put out into the world**, but it doesn’t make sense for us to "
"take on the responsibility of writing or maintaining documentation for "
"anything else."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../introduction/external-documentation.rst:15
#: ea9eefb7aebe4443af42c0a403e1ddf7
msgid ""
"For example, Qubes OS may use a popular Linux distribution for an official :"
"doc:`template </user/templates/templates>`. However, it would not make sense "
"for a comparatively small project like ours, with modest funding and a lean "
"workforce, to attempt to document software belonging to a large, richly-"
"funded project with an army of paid and volunteer contributors, especially "
"when they probably already have documentation of their own. This is "
"particularly true when it comes to Linux in general. Although many users who "
"are new to Qubes are also new to Linux, it makes absolutely no sense for our "
"comparatively tiny project to try to document Linux in general when there is "
"already a plethora of documentation out there."
msgstr ""

